// =============================================================================
// Enterprise License Management System (ELMS) - team VFast
// Database design (DBML) - design status: TARGET, nothing implemented yet
//
// Sources: README.md, docs/01-research-top-down.md, docs/02-use-cases.md,
//          docs/03-invest-requirements.md (state of main on 2026-11-11).
// UCxx / BR-xx / Ax in the notes refer to those documents. Dxx refers to the
// decisions below; docs/database/README.md explains each one, the options
// considered, and the use case text that must change with it.
//
// Render: paste into https://dbdiagram.io or run `npx -p @dbml/cli dbml2sql
//         docs/database/elms.dbml --postgres` (validated with @dbml/cli 12.0.0).
//         Reference DDL: docs/database/schema.sql. ERD per group:
//         docs/database/diagrams/ (python docs/diagrams/ve_erd.py).
//
// Decisions agreed by the team:
//   D1. A "license" is a license plan (tier/SKU such as Microsoft 365 E3). Holders,
//       usage, budget lines, expenses, and recommendations point to the plan;
//       an entitlement line is one purchase of that plan.
//   D2. Employees (directory) and user accounts (login) are separate tables.
//   D3. Purchased quantity can optionally be split into quotas per unit
//       (entitlement_allocations). A line without quotas is shared.
//   D4. Budgets are yearly per unit (docs/02 UC05); the monthly allocation and
//       category caps of docs/04 are not modelled.
//
// Decisions PROPOSED after the audit of 2026-11-11, pending team confirmation:
//   D5.  Two cost views. Billed cost = expenses (invoice, cash). Effective cost =
//        BR-05 monthly cost, split to units in cost_allocations (BR-06). Budget
//        utilization (UC08) and cost per department (UC06, UC16) use the
//        effective, allocated view; UC07 and invoice reconciliation use billed.
//   D6.  Prepaid invoices stay billed on their date; the spread over months is
//        the effective cost of the entitlement line. expenses get an optional
//        service period.
//   D7.  Per-seat status needs per-subject usage. An aggregate-only usage source
//        leaves seats Not monitored (A9).
//   D8.  Collection completeness is tracked per plan, provider account, kind of
//        data, and day (collection_coverage). Detection runs only on complete days.
//   D9.  History is kept by freezing results, not by versioning master data:
//        daily snapshots, and cost_allocations frozen when a month closes.
//        No employee department history table in this phase.
//   D10. Every plan has an owner unit. Company-level results (unused, overuse)
//        belong to the owner unit or to the quota unit; a Manager sees only rows
//        of their own units (BR-16). This replaces the UC10/UC12 rule "a Manager
//        sees the licenses that have a holder in their units".
//   D11. A vendor has one or more provider accounts (tenant, organization,
//        billing account). Identities and provider ids are unique per account.
//   D12. One reporting currency (system_settings). Snapshots and allocations are
//        converted with the rate in force on their date and then frozen.
//   D13. Overuse of a Metered line with a quota = consumption over the validity
//        of the line above its quota; pay-as-you-go without quota never overuses.
//   D14. Months close automatically on a set day of the next month; an employee
//        marked left has their account disabled automatically.
//   D15. A recommendation may have an Unknown estimated saving; Done needs the
//        actual saving.
//
// Conventions:
//   - Target DBMS: PostgreSQL 15+. Surrogate keys are bigint identity columns;
//     every table has a single-column id so audit_logs can point to any row.
//   - Money is numeric(18,2) with an ISO 4217 currency beside it; amounts in
//     different currencies are only added through exchange_rates (BR-05, D12).
//   - Quantities are numeric(20,4) because one column serves seats, sessions,
//     tokens, and cores.
//   - A NULL figure means Unknown and is never read as 0 (BR-04, A4). NULL has
//     no second meaning: "unlimited" is its own flag (is_unlimited). A sum with
//     one Unknown part is Unknown, never the sum of the known parts (PostgreSQL
//     SUM skips NULL, so totals must check for NULL parts first).
//   - Master data is never deleted, only marked inactive or ended (BR-15), so
//     no foreign key cascades on delete.
//   - Where a row has an end date, the date alone says whether it is active
//     (contracts.ended_on, entitlement_lines.valid_to,
//     user_accounts.disabled_at); there is no status column beside it. End
//     dates are inclusive: the row is valid on its last day.
//   - Each daily figure has one owner table: Purchased and cost in
//     plan_daily_snapshots, seat counts in plan_unit_daily_snapshots, period
//     usage in usage_records, completeness in collection_coverage.
//     detection_results stores only the verdict.
//   - Confidence (BR-14, A9) is derived from the source, not stored:
//     api or log per subject = high; api or log aggregate, or import = medium;
//     manual = low.
//   - updated_at is set by the application (or a trigger) on every update;
//     the default only covers the insert.
//   - Rules DBML cannot express are written in the table notes:
//       "Partial unique"  = a unique index with WHERE and/or NULLS NOT DISTINCT,
//                           to be created in the migration
//       "App rule"        = cross-table rule enforced in the service, inside the
//                           transaction that changes the data
// =============================================================================

Project elms {
  database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
  Note: '''
    Enterprise License Management System (ELMS).
    Read-only toward providers (BR-01): every table here holds data inside ELMS;
    nothing in this schema is written back to a provider.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Enums
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Enum org_unit_type {
  pnl [note: 'P&L (subsidiary); top level']
  department [note: 'Department under exactly one P&L']
}

Enum employee_status {
  active
  left [note: 'No longer with the company; the account is disabled (D14), seats still held are a waste signal']
}

Enum permission_action {
  read
  write
}

Enum data_source {
  api [note: 'Collected by a connector from a provider API']
  log [note: 'Collected by a connector from logs (license server, VPN)']
  import [note: 'CSV file imported by Staff']
  manual [note: 'Typed in by Staff']
}

Enum license_archetype {
  allocation [note: 'Seat, named user, device']
  concurrent [note: 'Slot, floating, VPN session']
  metered [note: 'Token, request, credit, GB']
  capacity [note: 'Core, CPU, server, instance']
}

Enum commercial_term {
  pay_as_you_go
  monthly
  yearly
  multi_year
  prepaid_credit
  perpetual [note: 'Perpetual with maintenance; only maintenance counts as cost (BR-05)']
}

Enum data_kind {
  entitlement [note: 'Purchased quantity and validity']
  assignment [note: 'Who holds the license']
  usage [note: 'Activity, sessions, consumption, deployed units']
  expense [note: 'Billing data: expenses and invoices']
}

Enum usage_granularity {
  per_subject [note: 'Usage known per user, device, project, or key']
  aggregate [note: 'Only totals; seats stay Not monitored and are never listed per user (A9, D7)']
}

Enum subject_type {
  user
  device
  project
  api_key
  other
}

Enum usage_metric {
  active_subjects [note: 'Allocation, aggregate source only: number of active users in the period']
  peak_concurrent [note: 'Concurrent: peak simultaneous sessions in the period']
  denied_requests [note: 'Concurrent: session requests refused in the period']
  consumption [note: 'Metered: tokens, requests, credits, GB consumed in the period']
  deployed_units [note: 'Capacity: units deployed at the end of the period']
}

Enum sync_trigger {
  scheduled
  manual
  backfill [note: 'History loaded on the first connection (A5)']
}

Enum run_status {
  running
  success
  partial [note: 'Some data collected; collection_coverage says which plans are complete']
  failed [note: 'Nothing written; figures of that day stay Unknown, never 0 (A4)']
}

Enum coverage_status {
  complete [note: 'All data of this kind for the plan and account was collected for the day']
  partial [note: 'Some pages or subjects missing; treated as Unknown by detection']
  failed [note: 'Nothing collected; Unknown']
}

Enum import_status {
  previewed [note: 'Parsed and validated; nothing written yet']
  confirmed [note: 'Rows written']
  rejected [note: 'At least one invalid row; whole file refused']
}

Enum budget_plan_status {
  draft
  active
}

Enum period_status {
  open
  closed
}

Enum cost_bucket {
  unit [note: 'Cost carried by a P&L or department']
  unallocated [note: 'Cost of purchased seats nobody holds, or of usage with no known department (BR-06)']
  unknown_department [note: 'Cost of seats whose holder has no department (BR-06)']
}

Enum allocation_method {
  per_seat [note: 'Effective cost split evenly over purchased seats (BR-06)']
  per_usage [note: 'Non-seat plan: split by the usage of subjects with a known department (UC06)']
  direct [note: 'Pay-as-you-go: expenses of the month that name a unit go to that unit']
  none [note: 'No basis to split: the whole cost is Unallocated']
}

Enum detection_check {
  unused [note: 'Unassigned seats (UC10)']
  inactive [note: 'Seats in Inactive or No activity (UC11)']
  overuse [note: 'Use above entitlement (UC12, BR-07, D13)']
}

Enum detection_outcome {
  clear [note: 'Evaluated, nothing found; Compliant for the overuse check']
  flagged
  not_evaluated [note: 'Data missing or incomplete; never counted as clear or compliant']
}

Enum recommendation_type {
  reduce_seats
  downgrade_plan
  cancel
  reassign
}

Enum recommendation_status {
  proposed
  accepted
  rejected
  done
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Organization and access (UC19-UC22, UC24)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table org_units {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  parent_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'NULL for a P&L; the owning P&L for a department']
  unit_type org_unit_type [not null]
  name varchar(200) [not null]
  source data_source [not null, default: 'manual', note: 'import = loaded from HR data; the name is then read-only (UC20)']
  external_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Key of the unit in the HR source, if imported']
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (parent_id, name) [unique, name: 'uq_org_units_parent_name']
    unit_type
  }

  checks {
    `(unit_type = 'pnl' and parent_id is null) or (unit_type = 'department' and parent_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_org_units_two_levels']
    `parent_id is null or parent_id <> id` [name: 'chk_org_units_not_own_parent']
  }

  Note: '''
    P&Ls (subsidiaries) and their departments in one two-level tree (UC20).
    A "unit" in the docs is one row of this table.
    Partial unique: P&L names are unique, case-insensitive
    (unique on lower(name) where parent_id is null).
    App rule: the parent of a department is a P&L (with the check above this
    also rules out deeper trees and cycles); a unit with active employees, an
    active budget plan, or active plans it owns cannot be marked inactive.
  '''
}

Table employees {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  employee_code varchar(50) [unique, note: 'HR code, if known']
  full_name varchar(200) [not null]
  email varchar(320) [not null, unique, note: 'Company email, stored lowercase; the matching key for accounts and provider identities']
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Department (or P&L when no department). NULL = Unknown department (BR-06)']
  status employee_status [not null, default: 'active']
  source data_source [not null, default: 'manual']
  external_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Key of the person in the HR or IdP source']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    org_unit_id
  }

  checks {
    `email = lower(email)` [name: 'chk_employees_email_lowercase']
  }

  Note: '''
    Directory of real employees (decision D2). An employee may have no account.
    Cost allocation, data scope, and "Unknown department" all read org_unit_id
    here, never from the account. Only the current department is kept (D9):
    past months keep their department through the frozen snapshots and
    cost_allocations.
    App rule: setting status to left disables the account of the employee in
    the same transaction (D14).
  '''
}

Table roles {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  code varchar(30) [not null, unique, note: 'ADMIN, MANAGER, STAFF, EMPLOYEE']
  name varchar(100) [not null]
  description text

  Note: 'The four fixed roles (BR-17). Seeded; UC21 changes the role of a user, not this list.'
}

Table permissions {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  feature_code varchar(60) [not null, note: 'One per row of the role x feature matrix, e.g. contracts, expenses, budget_plan, recommendations']
  action permission_action [not null]
  description text

  indexes {
    (feature_code, action) [unique, name: 'uq_permissions_feature_action']
  }

  Note: 'Catalogue of what can be granted: feature x (read | write) (UC22). Seeded.'
}

Table role_permissions {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  role_id bigint [not null, ref: > roles.id]
  permission_id bigint [not null, ref: > permissions.id]
  granted_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  granted_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (role_id, permission_id) [unique, name: 'uq_role_permissions_role_permission']
  }

  Note: '''
    Permission matrix; permissions belong to roles, never to single users (BR-17).
    App rule: Employee cannot be granted price or cost features; the permission
    Admin needs to manage permissions cannot be removed (UC22). Every change is
    written to audit_logs with its reason.
  '''
}

Table user_accounts {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  employee_id bigint [not null, unique, ref: - employees.id, note: 'Every account belongs to one employee; login email = employees.email']
  role_id bigint [not null, ref: > roles.id, note: 'Exactly one role per account (BR-17)']
  password_hash varchar(255) [note: 'Hashed, never plain (BR-18). NULL until a first password is set; login is refused']
  failed_login_count int [not null, default: 0, note: 'Consecutive failures; reset on success']
  locked_until timestamptz [note: 'Set to now + 15 minutes after 5 failures in a row (BR-18)']
  last_login_at timestamptz
  disabled_at timestamptz [note: 'NULL = active. Set = disabled: cannot log in and open sessions are revoked (UC19); cleared on re-enable']
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    role_id
  }

  checks {
    `failed_login_count >= 0` [name: 'chk_user_accounts_failed_count']
  }

  Note: '''
    Login accounts (UC19, UC21, UC24). Accounts are disabled, never deleted.
    App rule: the last active Admin cannot be disabled or lose the Admin role;
    an Admin cannot disable themselves (BR-17). An account of an employee with
    status left cannot be re-enabled (D14). A role change away from MANAGER
    removes the rows of the account in manager_org_units.
  '''
}

Table user_sessions {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  user_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  token_hash char(64) [not null, unique, note: 'SHA-256 of the session id kept in the HttpOnly, Secure cookie']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  last_seen_at timestamptz
  expires_at timestamptz [not null]
  revoked_at timestamptz [note: 'Set on logout, on disable, and on role change']
  ip_address varchar(45)
  user_agent text

  indexes {
    user_account_id
    expires_at
  }

  checks {
    `expires_at > created_at` [name: 'chk_user_sessions_expiry']
  }

  Note: '''
    Server-side sessions, so disabling an account ends its open sessions at once
    (UC19, BR-18). A new session id is issued at login (no session fixation);
    expired and revoked rows are purged by a daily job. Cookie sessions need
    CSRF protection (SameSite cookie plus a CSRF token on writes).
  '''
}

Table manager_org_units {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  user_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id]
  assigned_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  assigned_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (user_account_id, org_unit_id) [unique, name: 'uq_manager_org_units_account_unit']
    org_unit_id
  }

  Note: '''
    Units a Manager is responsible for (UC20); the source of Manager data scope
    (BR-16). A P&L assignment covers the departments under it.
    App rule: the account has the MANAGER role.
  '''
}

Table system_settings {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  key varchar(60) [not null, unique]
  value text [not null]
  description text
  updated_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  Note: '''
    Global settings, seeded and changed only through a migration or by Admin:
      reporting_currency         VND (D12); budgets are in this currency
      inactivity_threshold_days  60 (BR-03)
      month_close_day            10: day of the next month a month closes (D14)
      raw_record_retention_days  180
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. License catalog, entitlements, contracts (UC01-UC04)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table vendors {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  name varchar(200) [not null, unique]
  website varchar(500)
  support_contact varchar(500)
  collection_method data_source [not null, default: 'manual', note: 'How this vendor data is normally collected (UC02)']
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  Note: '''
    Vendors / providers (UC02).
    App rule: a vendor with an active contract cannot be marked inactive;
    creating a vendor creates its default provider account.
  '''
}

Table provider_accounts {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  vendor_id bigint [not null, ref: > vendors.id]
  name varchar(200) [not null, note: 'e.g. "Microsoft 365 - VinFast tenant"; "Default" for a vendor without tenants']
  tenant_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Tenant, organization, or billing account id at the provider']
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'P&L that owns the account, if one does']
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (vendor_id, name) [unique, name: 'uq_provider_accounts_vendor_name']
    (vendor_id, tenant_ref) [unique, name: 'uq_provider_accounts_vendor_tenant']
  }

  Note: '''
    One tenant, organization, or billing account at a provider (decision D11).
    A group of companies often has one Microsoft 365 tenant per P&L; user ids,
    subscription ids, and billing ids are unique only inside one account.
    Every vendor has at least one account; a vendor without tenants has one
    account named "Default".
  '''
}

Table software_categories {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  parent_id bigint [ref: > software_categories.id, note: 'NULL = category; set = subcategory of that category']
  name varchar(100) [not null]

  indexes {
    (parent_id, name) [unique, name: 'uq_software_categories_parent_name']
  }

  checks {
    `parent_id is null or parent_id <> id` [name: 'chk_software_categories_not_own_parent']
  }

  Note: '''
    Category and subcategory in a two-level tree.
    Partial unique: category names are unique where parent_id is null.
    App rule: the parent of a subcategory is a category (parent_id is null).
  '''
}

Table software_products {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  vendor_id bigint [not null, ref: > vendors.id]
  category_id bigint [ref: > software_categories.id, note: 'Most specific node (subcategory if any). NULL is shown as Uncategorized']
  name varchar(200) [not null]
  description text
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (vendor_id, name) [unique, name: 'uq_software_products_vendor_name']
    category_id
  }

  Note: '''
    Software catalog (UC01), e.g. Microsoft 365. The "License" column of most
    screens is this name; the "Plan" column is license_plans.name.
    The migration makes the name unique case-insensitive (on lower(name)).
    App rule: a product with an active entitlement line cannot be marked inactive.
  '''
}

Table product_links {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  product_id bigint [not null, ref: > software_products.id]
  label varchar(100) [not null]
  url varchar(1000) [not null]
  sort_order int [not null, default: 0]

  indexes {
    product_id
  }

  Note: 'Useful links of a product (UC01): policy, terms of service, admin portal.'
}

Table license_plans {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  product_id bigint [not null, ref: > software_products.id]
  name varchar(200) [not null, note: 'Tier / SKU name, e.g. E3, E5, Business, API pay-as-you-go']
  archetype license_archetype [not null, note: 'Measurement archetype (BR-02); every entitlement line of the plan inherits it']
  unit varchar(30) [not null, note: 'What is counted: seat, device, slot, token, credit, GB, core ...']
  owner_org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Unit that owns the license: receives its company-level results (D10)']
  description text
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (product_id, name) [unique, name: 'uq_license_plans_product_name']
    archetype
    owner_org_unit_id
  }

  Note: '''
    The unit everything else calls "a license" (decision D1): one tier of a
    product with one archetype and one unit. It stays the same across renewals,
    so holders, usage, budget lines, expenses, and recommendations survive a
    renewal. Purchased = sum of the entitlement lines of the plan that are
    active on that day (see entitlement_lines).
    Holders and usage are kept per plan, not per line (D1): providers pool the
    seats of several purchases.
    The owner unit (D10) is usually the P&L or IT department that buys the
    license; Managers of that unit see its unassigned seats, overuse, and
    holders with Unknown department. The migration makes the name unique
    case-insensitive (on product_id, lower(name)).
  '''
}

Table contracts {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  vendor_id bigint [not null, ref: > vendors.id]
  contract_no varchar(100) [note: 'Number on the vendor paper, if any']
  title varchar(200) [not null]
  start_date date [not null]
  renewal_date date
  notice_period_days int [not null, default: 0]
  auto_renew boolean [not null, default: false]
  commitment_amount numeric(18,2) [note: 'Minimum commitment of the agreement, if any']
  total_value numeric(18,2)
  currency char(3)
  ended_on date [note: 'NULL = not ended. Set by "mark ended" (UC04)']
  attachment_file_id bigint [ref: > files.id]
  notes text
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (vendor_id, contract_no) [unique, name: 'uq_contracts_vendor_no']
    renewal_date
    ended_on
  }

  checks {
    `renewal_date is null or renewal_date >= start_date` [name: 'chk_contracts_renewal_after_start']
    `ended_on is null or ended_on >= start_date` [name: 'chk_contracts_ended_after_start']
    `notice_period_days >= 0` [name: 'chk_contracts_notice_period']
    `(total_value is null and commitment_amount is null) or currency is not null` [name: 'chk_contracts_currency']
    `commitment_amount is null or commitment_amount >= 0` [name: 'chk_contracts_commitment']
    `total_value is null or total_value >= 0` [name: 'chk_contracts_total_value']
  }

  Note: '''
    Contracts (UC04). A contract is active on a day when start_date <= day and
    ended_on is null or later; there is no status column.
    Computed, not stored:
      Notice deadline       = renewal_date - notice_period_days: the last day to
                              tell the vendor before an auto-renewal (UC13)
      Renewal soon          = renewal_date within 30 days
      Notice period passed  = today > notice deadline
    Renewal dates feed the forecast (UC09) and recommendation timing (UC13).
  '''
}

Table entitlement_lines {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  provider_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > provider_accounts.id, note: 'Account the purchase belongs to (D11)']
  contract_id bigint [ref: > contracts.id, note: 'Contract covering this line; one FK means a line is never under two contracts (UC04)']
  renews_line_id bigint [ref: > entitlement_lines.id, note: 'The line this one renews, if any; keeps the renewal chain']
  quantity numeric(20,4) [note: 'Purchased quantity or quota. NULL = Unknown, unless is_unlimited']
  is_unlimited boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'True for a line bought without a quota (e.g. metered pay-as-you-go): quantity is NULL and the line can never be over-used (BR-07)']
  valid_from date [not null]
  valid_to date [note: 'Last day of validity, inclusive. NULL = open-ended (perpetual). "End a line" (UC03) sets this date']
  commercial_term commercial_term [not null, note: 'The one field for how the line is paid (BR-02); it also fixes the period of unit_price']
  unit_price numeric(18,4) [note: 'Price of one unit for the period of the commercial term (see table note). NULL = Unknown']
  currency char(3) [not null]
  source data_source [not null, default: 'manual', note: 'Source of quantity and validity (BR-14); prices always come from Staff']
  external_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Subscription id at the provider, if synced']
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, valid_from, valid_to)
    provider_account_id
    contract_id
    renews_line_id
  }

  checks {
    `quantity is null or quantity >= 0` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_quantity']
    `not is_unlimited or quantity is null` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_unlimited']
    `valid_to is null or valid_to >= valid_from` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_validity']
    `unit_price is null or unit_price >= 0` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_unit_price']
    `renews_line_id is null or renews_line_id <> id` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_not_own_renewal']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_entitlement_lines_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    One purchase of a plan (UC03): quantity, validity, and price terms.
    A renewal or an extra purchase is a new line under the same plan.
    A line is active on a day when valid_from <= day and (valid_to is null or
    valid_to >= day). There is no status column: ending a line sets valid_to.
    A renewal starts the day after the line it renews ends, so the boundary day
    is never counted twice.
    unit_price and effective monthly cost (BR-05) by commercial term:
      monthly            price per unit per month       quantity x unit_price
      yearly, multi_year price per unit per year        quantity x unit_price / 12
      perpetual          maintenance per unit per year  quantity x unit_price / 12
      prepaid_credit     price per credit               quantity x unit_price /
                                                        months of validity
      pay_as_you_go      reference rate per unit        actual spend of the
                                                        month from expenses
    Quarterly payment is entered as its yearly price.
    Partial unique: one line per subscription at the provider
    (unique on provider_account_id, external_ref where external_ref is not null),
    so a re-run sync updates the line instead of adding one (A3).
    App rule: the vendor of the account and of the contract equals the vendor
    of the plan product; a renewal line belongs to the same plan and starts
    after the renewed line ends. A connector value edited by Staff needs a row
    in data_overrides (BR-14).
  '''
}

Table entitlement_allocations {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  entitlement_line_id bigint [not null, ref: > entitlement_lines.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id]
  quantity numeric(20,4) [not null]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (entitlement_line_id, org_unit_id) [unique, name: 'uq_entitlement_allocations_line_unit']
    org_unit_id
  }

  checks {
    `quantity > 0` [name: 'chk_entitlement_allocations_quantity']
  }

  Note: '''
    Optional quota of a purchase per unit (decision D3); gives the "Purchased"
    level per unit in budget monitoring (UC08, BR-09) and the unit of its
    unassigned seats (D10).
    A line with no rows is shared: its seats belong to the owner unit of the
    plan for detection, and no "Unassigned" gap is flagged per unit (BR-04).
    Quotas apply for the whole validity of the line; a different split is a new
    line. History per day is kept in plan_unit_daily_snapshots.
    App rule: quotas are allowed only on a line with a known quantity that is
    not unlimited, and add up to at most that quantity; the service locks the
    line row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) before checking, so two concurrent changes
    cannot exceed it.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 3. Collection pipeline (principles A1-A9, UC03 imports, UC07 imports)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table connectors {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  provider_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > provider_accounts.id]
  name varchar(200) [not null, unique]
  connector_type varchar(60) [not null, note: 'Implementation key, e.g. ms_graph, license_server_log; it also says whether the connector reads an API or a log']
  base_url varchar(500)
  credentials_ref text [note: 'Reference to the secret in the secret store, or the credentials encrypted with a key kept outside the database; read-only scopes only (A8)']
  schedule_cron varchar(100) [not null, default: '0 2 * * *', note: 'Daily by default (A1)']
  is_simulated boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'True when the connector reads a fake provider, so figures are not presented as real (A9)']
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    provider_account_id
  }

  Note: '''
    One read-only connection to one provider account. The Admin configuration
    screen is a later phase (docs/01 section 7), so rows are seeded for now.
  '''
}

Table plan_data_sources {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  provider_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > provider_accounts.id]
  data_type data_kind [not null]
  source_type data_source [not null, note: 'Stamped as source on every row collected for this plan, account, and kind of data']
  connector_id bigint [ref: > connectors.id, note: 'Required when source_type is api or log']
  external_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Key of the plan at the provider, e.g. Microsoft Graph skuId']
  granularity usage_granularity [note: 'Required for usage: per subject or aggregate only']
  monitoring_since date [not null, default: `current_date`, note: 'First day this source delivered data; Inactive needs a full threshold of monitoring (D7)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, provider_account_id, data_type) [unique, name: 'uq_plan_data_sources_plan_account_type']
    connector_id
  }

  checks {
    `(source_type in ('api', 'log')) = (connector_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_plan_data_sources_connector']
    `(data_type = 'usage') = (granularity is not null)` [name: 'chk_plan_data_sources_granularity']
  }

  Note: '''
    The one primary source of each kind of data for a plan in one provider
    account (BR-14).
    - A plan whose assignment or usage source is a connector refuses manual
      entry and import of that data (UC03).
    - A plan with no "usage" row for an account, or with an aggregate one, has
      no per-seat usage there: its seats are "Not monitored" (BR-03, D7) and
      are never counted as waste (BR-04).
    App rule: the connector reads the same provider account.
  '''
}

Table sync_runs {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  connector_id bigint [not null, ref: > connectors.id]
  trigger sync_trigger [not null, default: 'scheduled']
  status run_status [not null, default: 'running']
  data_date date [not null, note: 'The day the collected figures describe (reports lag 1-2 days)']
  window_start timestamptz [note: 'Incremental window (A3)']
  window_end timestamptz
  records_read int [not null, default: 0]
  records_written int [not null, default: 0]
  error_message text
  started_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  finished_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (connector_id, data_date)
    status
  }

  checks {
    `(status = 'running') = (finished_at is null)` [name: 'chk_sync_runs_finished']
    `finished_at is null or finished_at >= started_at` [name: 'chk_sync_runs_duration']
    `window_end is null or window_start is null or window_end >= window_start` [name: 'chk_sync_runs_window']
  }

  Note: '''
    One execution of a connector. A failed run writes no figures, so that day
    stays Unknown instead of 0 (A4, BR-04); the next run catches up (A3).
    Which plans a run covered completely is in collection_coverage.
    A backfill writes one run per data date.
  '''
}

Table collection_coverage {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  provider_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > provider_accounts.id]
  data_type data_kind [not null]
  data_date date [not null]
  status coverage_status [not null]
  sync_run_id bigint [not null, ref: > sync_runs.id, note: 'Latest run that wrote this day']
  error_code varchar(60)
  collected_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, provider_account_id, data_type, data_date) [unique, name: 'uq_collection_coverage_plan_account_type_date']
    (data_date, status)
    sync_run_id
  }

  Note: '''
    Whether the connector data of a plan, account, and kind is complete for a
    day (decision D8). A connector run writes one row per plan and kind it
    collects; a later run of the same day replaces the row.
    No row, partial, or failed = Unknown for that day: detection reports
    not_evaluated (UC10-UC12, UC17) and daily snapshots are not written.
    A successful run that finds 0 holders writes complete, so a true 0 is
    told apart from a missing day.
    Manual and imported data has no daily coverage: it is as of its last entry
    or confirmed import, with low or medium confidence (BR-14).
  '''
}

Table raw_records {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  sync_run_id bigint [not null, ref: > sync_runs.id]
  record_type varchar(60) [not null, note: 'Provider object, e.g. subscribedSku, user, activeUserDetail']
  external_id varchar(200)
  payload jsonb [not null]
  payload_hash char(64) [not null, note: 'SHA-256 of the payload, to skip normalizing unchanged records']
  fetched_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  normalized_at timestamptz [note: 'NULL until normalized into the tables below']

  indexes {
    (sync_run_id, record_type)
    (record_type, external_id)
  }

  Note: '''
    Raw provider data kept before normalization, so rules can change and be
    recomputed without calling the API again (A2).
    Payloads hold personal data (names, emails): only the collection service
    reads this table, and rows older than raw_record_retention_days
    (system_settings) are deleted. Idempotency is ensured by the unique keys of
    the normalized tables, not by payload_hash.
  '''
}

Table files {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  storage_key varchar(500) [not null, unique, note: 'Path or object key in file storage; the bytes are not in the database']
  original_name varchar(255) [not null]
  content_type varchar(100) [not null]
  size_bytes bigint [not null]
  checksum char(64) [not null, note: 'SHA-256 of the content']
  uploaded_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  uploaded_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  checks {
    `size_bytes > 0 and size_bytes <= 10485760` [name: 'chk_files_size']
  }

  Note: '''
    Uploaded files: contract attachments, expense invoices (PDF or image, at
    most 10 MB, BR-10), and CSV import files. The service checks the content
    type from the bytes, not from the name; files are served only through the
    API with the permission of the row they belong to.
  '''
}

Table import_batches {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  import_type data_kind [not null]
  license_plan_id bigint [ref: > license_plans.id, note: 'Set for assignment and usage imports, which target one plan']
  provider_account_id bigint [ref: > provider_accounts.id, note: 'Set for assignment and usage imports: the account the holders belong to']
  file_id bigint [not null, ref: > files.id]
  status import_status [not null, default: 'previewed']
  rows_total int [not null, default: 0]
  rows_added int [not null, default: 0]
  rows_updated int [not null, default: 0]
  rows_rejected int [not null, default: 0]
  error_report jsonb [note: 'Rejected rows with their errors']
  imported_by bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  confirmed_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (import_type, created_at)
    license_plan_id
  }

  checks {
    `(status = 'confirmed') = (confirmed_at is not null)` [name: 'chk_import_batches_confirmed']
    `(import_type in ('assignment', 'usage')) = (license_plan_id is not null and provider_account_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_import_batches_target']
  }

  Note: '''
    One CSV import by Staff: preview, then confirm (UC03, UC07). This is the
    entry history "who, when, file, rows". One invalid row rejects the file.
    App rule: confirm re-validates the same file (checksum) against the current
    data and refuses when the preview is older than 1 hour or the plan has
    gained a connector source since.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 4. Holders, usage, and history (UC03, UC06, UC10-UC12, UC15, UC23)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table subjects {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  provider_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > provider_accounts.id, note: 'Identities are unique per account (D11)']
  subject_type subject_type [not null, default: 'user']
  identifier varchar(320) [not null, note: 'Provider identity, lowercase: email / userPrincipalName, device name, project, key label']
  external_id varchar(200) [note: 'Immutable id at the provider, if any; survives a rename of the identifier']
  display_name varchar(200)
  employee_id bigint [ref: > employees.id, note: 'Only for user subjects. Matched by company email. NULL = not matched: shown with the provider identity and Unknown department']
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Only for non-person subjects (project, key, device pool) whose department is known (UC06)']
  is_enabled boolean [note: 'Account enabled at the provider; NULL = Unknown']
  source data_source [not null]
  first_seen_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  last_seen_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (provider_account_id, subject_type, identifier) [unique, name: 'uq_subjects_account_type_identifier']
    employee_id
    org_unit_id
  }

  checks {
    `employee_id is null or org_unit_id is null` [name: 'chk_subjects_one_department_source']
    `subject_type = 'user' or employee_id is null` [name: 'chk_subjects_employee_only_user']
    `identifier = lower(identifier)` [name: 'chk_subjects_identifier_lowercase']
  }

  Note: '''
    Who or what uses a license on the provider side: a user account, a device,
    a project, an API key. Kept apart from employees because a provider identity
    may match no employee (UC03, UC11).
    Department of a subject = employees.org_unit_id for a matched user,
    otherwise subjects.org_unit_id, otherwise Unknown department.
    Partial unique: unique on provider_account_id, external_id where external_id
    is not null; a sync matches on external_id first, so a renamed user keeps
    the same subject and seat history.
    Matching to an employee uses the company email first; Staff can confirm a
    match by hand for an alias or a UPN that differs from the email.
  '''
}

Table license_assignments {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  subject_id bigint [not null, ref: > subjects.id]
  entitlement_line_id bigint [ref: > entitlement_lines.id, note: 'Purchase the seat belongs to. Set on Staff entry and by a sync when the plan has one active line in the account. NULL = not known: the provider pools the seats of several purchases']
  assigned_on date [note: 'Assigned date reported by the provider or entered by Staff; NULL = Unknown']
  first_seen_on date [not null, note: 'First day ELMS saw the assignment']
  ended_on date [note: 'NULL = currently assigned']
  last_active_at timestamptz [note: 'Last recorded activity; NULL = no activity recorded. Only filled from a per-subject usage source']
  source data_source [not null]
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  entered_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, ended_on)
    subject_id
    entitlement_line_id
    last_active_at
  }

  checks {
    `ended_on is null or ended_on >= first_seen_on` [name: 'chk_license_assignments_dates']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_license_assignments_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_license_assignments_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    A holder of a plan: "Assigned" data read from the provider or entered by
    Staff; ELMS never assigns or revokes (BR-01). An ended assignment keeps its
    row.
    Partial unique: one open assignment per plan and subject
    (unique on license_plan_id, subject_id where ended_on is null).
    Seat status (BR-03, D7) is computed, not stored, for an open assignment.
    S = the usage source of the plan for the account of the subject,
    T = inactivity_threshold_days (60):
      Not monitored = no S, or S.granularity = aggregate
      Active        = last_active_at within the last T days
      Inactive      = last_active_at older than T days
      No activity   = last_active_at is null
    Detection (UC11) flags Inactive and No activity only when, on the data
    date, the usage coverage is complete, S.monitoring_since is at least T days
    old, and the seat has been held for at least T days (from assigned_on, or
    first_seen_on when unknown). A new seat is not waste yet.
    Unassigned = purchased quantity minus open assignments.
    Expiry date of a seat (UC23) and its contract (UC13):
      entitlement_line_id set  = valid_to and contract of that line
      entitlement_line_id NULL = the earliest valid_to among the active lines
                                 of the plan in the account, the first day the
                                 seat may lapse
    App rule: the line belongs to the same plan and the same provider account
    as the subject.
  '''
}

Table usage_records {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  provider_account_id bigint [not null, ref: > provider_accounts.id]
  subject_id bigint [ref: > subjects.id, note: 'NULL = aggregate figure for the whole plan in the account']
  metric usage_metric [not null]
  period_start date [not null]
  period_end date [not null, note: 'Inclusive']
  quantity numeric(20,4) [not null]
  source data_source [not null]
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  entered_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, provider_account_id, subject_id, metric, period_start, period_end) [unique, name: 'uq_usage_records_period']
    (license_plan_id, metric, period_start)
    subject_id
  }

  checks {
    `period_end >= period_start` [name: 'chk_usage_records_period']
    `quantity >= 0` [name: 'chk_usage_records_quantity']
    `metric <> 'active_subjects' or subject_id is null` [name: 'chk_usage_records_active_subjects_aggregate']
    `metric not in ('active_subjects', 'peak_concurrent', 'denied_requests') or quantity = trunc(quantity)` [name: 'chk_usage_records_whole_counts']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_usage_records_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_usage_records_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    Usage per period for Concurrent, Metered, and Capacity plans, and aggregate
    activity for Allocation plans without per-user data. Per-user activity of a
    seat lives in license_assignments.last_active_at.
    Entering the same period again replaces the row (UC03): the unique index
    must be created with NULLS NOT DISTINCT so it also holds for aggregate rows,
    where subject_id is NULL.
    App rule: one period length per plan, account, and metric (the period of
    the source, usually a day or a month) and no overlapping periods, so sums
    over periods never count a day twice. The metric matches the archetype of
    the plan (see the enum notes).
    Metered overuse (D13) = sum of consumption over the validity of a line
    with a quota, compared with that quota.
    A missing period is Unknown, never 0 (BR-04).
  '''
}

Table plan_daily_snapshots {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  snapshot_date date [not null]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  purchased_qty numeric(20,4) [note: 'Sum of the entitlement lines active that day; NULL = Unknown (one active line Unknown makes the sum Unknown), or unlimited']
  is_unlimited boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'True when an active line of the plan is unlimited; purchased_qty is then NULL']
  effective_monthly_cost numeric(18,2) [note: 'BR-05 cost of a full month at the terms in force that day, in the reporting currency; NULL = Unknown (price or exchange rate missing)']
  currency char(3) [not null, note: 'Reporting currency (D12)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (snapshot_date, license_plan_id) [unique, name: 'uq_plan_daily_snapshots_date_plan']
    license_plan_id
  }

  checks {
    `not is_unlimited or purchased_qty is null` [name: 'chk_plan_daily_snapshots_unlimited']
  }

  Note: '''
    Daily Purchased and cost per plan, kept by ELMS because providers give no
    history (docs/01 section 4.4) and because a sync or a Staff correction
    overwrites the quantity of a line, so past days cannot be recomputed from
    entitlement_lines. Feeds trends, the forecast, and cost_allocations.
    Rows are frozen once written; a later rate or price correction changes only
    new days (D9, D12). Amounts are converted with the latest exchange rate
    whose effective_from is on or before the snapshot date.
    effective_monthly_cost is a monthly rate, not a daily amount: the cost of a
    month = sum over its days of effective_monthly_cost / days in the month.
    Never add up the daily rows as they are.
    Assigned and Used are not stored here, so each figure has one owner:
    seat counts are the sum over units of plan_unit_daily_snapshots; peak,
    consumption, and deployed units of non-seat plans are in usage_records.
    No row or a NULL column = Unknown for that day.
  '''
}

Table plan_unit_daily_snapshots {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  snapshot_date date [not null]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Department of the holders that day; NULL = Unknown department']
  assigned_count int [not null]
  active_count int [not null]
  inactive_count int [not null]
  no_activity_count int [not null]
  not_monitored_count int [not null]
  used_qty numeric(20,4) [note: 'Non-seat plans: consumption or peak attributed to the unit; NULL = Unknown']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (snapshot_date, license_plan_id, org_unit_id) [unique, name: 'uq_plan_unit_daily_snapshots']
    (license_plan_id, snapshot_date)
    (org_unit_id, snapshot_date)
  }

  checks {
    `assigned_count = active_count + inactive_count + no_activity_count + not_monitored_count` [name: 'chk_plan_unit_daily_snapshots_sum']
    `active_count >= 0 and inactive_count >= 0 and no_activity_count >= 0 and not_monitored_count >= 0` [name: 'chk_plan_unit_daily_snapshots_counts']
  }

  Note: '''
    Daily seat status per plan and department: every assigned seat has exactly
    one status (BR-03), so the four counts add up to assigned_count. The
    department is the one of that day, so history keeps it after an employee
    moves (D9).
    Feeds the monthly usage charts, "Assigned" / "Used" per unit (BR-09), and
    the seat basis of cost_allocations.
    The unique index needs NULLS NOT DISTINCT because org_unit_id may be NULL.
    Rows are written only for a day whose assignment coverage is complete in
    every account of the plan (D8); counts have no default, so a missing day is
    no row, never a row of zeros.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 5. Budget, cost, and expenses (UC05-UC09, UC16)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table budget_plans {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  org_unit_id bigint [not null, ref: > org_units.id]
  fiscal_year int [not null]
  budget_amount numeric(18,2) [not null]
  currency char(3) [not null, note: 'Reporting currency (D12)']
  note text
  status budget_plan_status [not null, default: 'draft']
  activated_at timestamptz
  activated_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_by bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (org_unit_id, fiscal_year) [unique, name: 'uq_budget_plans_unit_year']
    (fiscal_year, status)
  }

  checks {
    `budget_amount > 0` [name: 'chk_budget_plans_amount']
    `(status = 'active') = (activated_at is not null and activated_by is not null)` [name: 'chk_budget_plans_activation']
  }

  Note: '''
    Yearly license budget of one unit (UC05, BR-08, decision D4): at most one
    plan per unit and fiscal year; only active plans count.
    P&L and department plans are two separate levels and are never added
    together (UC08, UC16): a P&L plan is the envelope for the whole P&L, the
    plans of its departments are shares inside it.
      Company total = the P&L plans; for a P&L without its own plan, the sum
                      of its department plans.
      Inside a P&L  = P&L budget minus the sum of its department budgets is
                      shown as "Not distributed".
    Actual cost against the budget = the cost_allocations of the unit in the
    fiscal year (effective, allocated view, D5); for a P&L, its own rows plus
    those of its departments.
    App rule: activation shows a warning and needs confirmation when the plan
    lines add up to more than the budget, or when the department budgets of a
    P&L add up to more than the P&L budget (UC05).
    App rule: only a draft can be deleted. A change to an active plan needs a
    reason and is written to audit_logs with old and new value (BR-08).
    App rule: the currency is the reporting currency.
  '''
}

Table budget_plan_lines {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  budget_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > budget_plans.id]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  planned_quantity numeric(20,4) [not null]
  planned_cost numeric(18,2) [not null, note: 'In the currency of the budget plan; suggested = quantity x current yearly unit price, converted with the current rate']
  note text
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (budget_plan_id, license_plan_id) [unique, name: 'uq_budget_plan_lines_plan_license']
    license_plan_id
  }

  checks {
    `planned_quantity >= 0` [name: 'chk_budget_plan_lines_quantity']
    `planned_cost >= 0` [name: 'chk_budget_plan_lines_cost']
  }

  Note: 'Plan lines: the "Planned" level of the reconciliation chain Planned -> Purchased -> Assigned -> Used -> Actual cost (BR-09).'
}

Table cost_allocations {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  accounting_period_id bigint [not null, ref: > accounting_periods.id]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  bucket cost_bucket [not null]
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Set when bucket = unit']
  method allocation_method [not null]
  basis_qty numeric(20,4) [note: 'Average seats held (per_seat) or usage (per_usage) of the bucket in the month; NULL for direct and none']
  amount numeric(18,2) [note: 'Share of the plan cost of the month; NULL = Unknown (price, rate, or seat data missing)']
  currency char(3) [not null, note: 'Reporting currency (D12)']
  is_final boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'Set when the month closes; a final row is never recomputed']
  computed_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (accounting_period_id, license_plan_id, bucket, org_unit_id) [unique, name: 'uq_cost_allocations_period_plan_bucket_unit']
    (org_unit_id, accounting_period_id)
    license_plan_id
  }

  checks {
    `(bucket = 'unit') = (org_unit_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_cost_allocations_unit_bucket']
    `basis_qty is null or basis_qty >= 0` [name: 'chk_cost_allocations_basis']
  }

  Note: '''
    Effective cost of a plan for one month, split to units (UC06, BR-06,
    decision D5). Source of "cost per department" (UC06, UC16) and of the
    actual cost in budget monitoring (UC08).
    Plan cost of the month:
      fixed terms     sum over the days of plan_daily_snapshots
                      .effective_monthly_cost / days in the month
      pay_as_you_go   expenses of the plan whose service period (or date)
                      falls in the month
    Split, by method:
      per_seat   cost / average purchased seats x average seats of the unit
                 (plan_unit_daily_snapshots); unheld seats go to unallocated,
                 holders without department to unknown_department
      per_usage  by the usage of subjects with a known department; the rest
                 is unallocated
      direct     pay-as-you-go expenses that name a unit go to that unit; the
                 rest is unallocated
      none       the whole cost is unallocated
    The rows of a plan and month add up to the plan cost (UC06 result).
    Rows of an open month are recomputed daily; on month close they are
    computed once more and marked final, so a later move of an employee, a
    corrected rate, or a changed rule never rewrites a closed month (D9).
    The unique index needs NULLS NOT DISTINCT because org_unit_id may be NULL.
  '''
}

Table expenses {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  expense_date date [not null, note: 'Invoice or charge date; decides the closed month (BR-10)']
  service_period_start date [note: 'First day of the service the expense pays for, if known (D6)']
  service_period_end date [note: 'Last day of that service, inclusive']
  amount numeric(18,2) [not null, note: 'Positive; only a correcting entry may be negative']
  currency char(3) [not null]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Unit that pays the invoice (BR-10). Required on manual entry and CSV; NULL only for billing API rows without a unit, shown as Unallocated']
  description text
  invoice_file_id bigint [ref: > files.id]
  corrects_expense_id bigint [ref: > expenses.id, note: 'Set on a correcting entry for an expense of a closed month (BR-10)']
  provider_account_id bigint [ref: > provider_accounts.id, note: 'Billing account the record came from; set for api rows']
  source data_source [not null, default: 'manual']
  external_ref varchar(200) [note: 'Id of the billing record at the provider, for idempotent sync (A3)']
  sync_run_id bigint [ref: > sync_runs.id]
  import_batch_id bigint [ref: > import_batches.id]
  created_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    expense_date
    (license_plan_id, expense_date)
    (org_unit_id, expense_date)
    corrects_expense_id
  }

  checks {
    `amount <> 0` [name: 'chk_expenses_amount_not_zero']
    `amount > 0 or corrects_expense_id is not null` [name: 'chk_expenses_negative_only_correction']
    `corrects_expense_id is null or corrects_expense_id <> id` [name: 'chk_expenses_not_own_correction']
    `source in ('api', 'log') or org_unit_id is not null` [name: 'chk_expenses_unit_required']
    `(service_period_start is null) = (service_period_end is null)` [name: 'chk_expenses_service_period_pair']
    `service_period_end is null or service_period_end >= service_period_start` [name: 'chk_expenses_service_period']
    `external_ref is null or provider_account_id is not null` [name: 'chk_expenses_external_ref_account']
    `(source in ('api', 'log')) = (sync_run_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_expenses_sync_provenance']
    `(source = 'import') = (import_batch_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_expenses_import_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
    Expenses and invoices (UC07): the billed cost view (D5), used for invoice
    reconciliation, cash, and the "Billed" figures of the financial dashboard.
    The vendor is read through the plan and product.
    A prepaid invoice stays on its expense_date; its spread over months is the
    effective cost of the entitlement line, not a split of this row (D6).
    Pay-as-you-go expenses are also the cost source of cost_allocations.
    Partial unique: one row per billing record
    (unique on provider_account_id, external_ref where external_ref is not null).
    App rule: an expense is editable until its month is closed
    (accounting_periods); afterwards only a correcting entry is allowed, and it
    is dated in an open month. An expense that came from a billing API needs a
    reason to be edited (BR-14).
  '''
}

Table accounting_periods {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  fiscal_year int [not null]
  period_year int [not null]
  period_month int [not null]
  status period_status [not null, default: 'open']
  closed_at timestamptz
  closed_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id, note: 'NULL when closed by the system job']

  indexes {
    (period_year, period_month) [unique, name: 'uq_accounting_periods_month']
    (fiscal_year, status)
  }

  checks {
    `period_month between 1 and 12` [name: 'chk_accounting_periods_month']
    `(status = 'closed') = (closed_at is not null)` [name: 'chk_accounting_periods_closed']
  }

  Note: '''
    Calendar months and whether they are closed. A closed month locks its
    expenses (BR-10), freezes its cost_allocations (D9), and counts as a
    "closed month" for the forecast run rate (BR-11). fiscal_year maps the
    month to a budget year.
    Closing (D14): a system job closes month M on month_close_day of M+1
    (system_settings, default the 10th); Staff can close it earlier. A closed
    month is never reopened; later changes are correcting entries.
  '''
}

Table exchange_rates {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  from_currency char(3) [not null]
  to_currency char(3) [not null]
  rate numeric(18,8) [not null, note: '1 from_currency = rate to_currency']
  effective_from date [not null]
  declared_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (from_currency, to_currency, effective_from) [unique, name: 'uq_exchange_rates_pair_date']
  }

  checks {
    `rate > 0` [name: 'chk_exchange_rates_rate']
    `from_currency <> to_currency` [name: 'chk_exchange_rates_pair']
  }

  Note: '''
    Declared exchange rates (BR-05, D12), always toward the reporting currency.
    The rate of a day = the row with the latest effective_from on or before that
    day. Without a rate, converted figures are Unknown and amounts are shown per
    currency, never added (UC16).
    A corrected rate changes only figures not yet frozen; frozen snapshots and
    final cost_allocations keep the rate they were computed with.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 6. Optimization (UC10-UC14, UC17, UC18)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table detection_runs {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  data_date date [not null, note: 'Date of the data the run evaluated']
  inactivity_threshold_days int [not null, default: 60, note: 'Copied from system_settings so old results stay explainable']
  rule_version varchar(20) [not null, note: 'Version of the detection rules, e.g. 2026.11']
  status run_status [not null, default: 'running']
  started_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  finished_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    data_date
  }

  checks {
    `(status = 'running') = (finished_at is null)` [name: 'chk_detection_runs_finished']
  }

  Note: 'One daily detection run (BR-12). A re-run for the same data date adds a new run; screens read the latest successful run.'
}

Table detection_results {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  detection_run_id bigint [not null, ref: > detection_runs.id]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Unit the result belongs to (D10). NULL only for inactive seats of holders with Unknown department']
  check_type detection_check [not null]
  outcome detection_outcome [not null]
  flagged_qty numeric(20,4) [note: 'Unassigned seats, inactive seats, or excess over the entitlement; 0 when clear; NULL when not evaluated']
  monthly_cost numeric(18,2) [note: 'Monthly cost of the flagged quantity; NULL = Unknown']
  currency char(3)
  flagged_since date [note: 'First day of the current unbroken flagged streak ("Since", UC12)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (detection_run_id, license_plan_id, check_type, org_unit_id) [unique, name: 'uq_detection_results_run_plan_check_unit']
    (check_type, outcome)
    license_plan_id
    org_unit_id
  }

  checks {
    `check_type = 'inactive' or org_unit_id is not null` [name: 'chk_detection_results_unit']
    `(outcome = 'not_evaluated') = (flagged_qty is null)` [name: 'chk_detection_results_not_evaluated']
    `outcome <> 'flagged' or flagged_qty > 0` [name: 'chk_detection_results_flagged']
    `outcome <> 'clear' or flagged_qty = 0` [name: 'chk_detection_results_clear']
    `(outcome = 'flagged') = (flagged_since is not null)` [name: 'chk_detection_results_since']
    `monthly_cost is null or currency is not null` [name: 'chk_detection_results_currency']
  }

  Note: '''
    Result of one check for one plan and unit in one run: only the verdict is
    stored (outcome, flagged quantity, its cost, since when).
    Unit of a result (D10):
      unused   one row per unit with a quota (quota minus its holders), and one
               row for the owner unit of the plan for the shared seats
      overuse  one row for the owner unit of the plan
      inactive one row per department of the holders; NULL = Unknown department
    Manager data scope (BR-16): a Manager sees the rows of their units, plus the
    Unknown-department rows of the plans their units own. No figure of another
    unit is shown.
    Lists, dashboards, and the compliance view read the same rows, so figures
    tie across screens (UC10, UC12, UC17, UC18).
    not_evaluated when the coverage of the data date is not complete (D8), or
    the figures needed are Unknown.
    The figures shown beside a result are read from their owner table for the
    data date of the run, never copied here:
      Purchased / Entitlement = plan_daily_snapshots.purchased_qty
                                (or the quota of the unit)
      Assigned, seat statuses = plan_unit_daily_snapshots
      Peak, deployed units    = usage_records
      Unassigned, Excess      = flagged_qty
    Evidence (BR-12) = these figures, last activity from license_assignments,
    and the data date. The per-seat list of UC11 is the current list of
    license_assignments: it is shown for the latest run only; older runs keep
    their counts, not the names.
    Saving opportunities (UC13) are computed from the latest results and the
    contract dates; they are not stored until turned into a recommendation.
    The unique index needs NULLS NOT DISTINCT because org_unit_id may be NULL.
  '''
}

Table recommendations {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  license_plan_id bigint [not null, ref: > license_plans.id]
  target_plan_id bigint [ref: > license_plans.id, note: 'For downgrade_plan: the plan to move to, of the same product']
  org_unit_id bigint [ref: > org_units.id, note: 'Unit the recommendation concerns, for Manager data scope (D10); NULL = holders with Unknown department']
  detection_result_id bigint [ref: > detection_results.id, note: 'Result it was created from; NULL when created by hand']
  type recommendation_type [not null]
  title varchar(300) [not null]
  description text
  evidence jsonb [not null, note: 'Snapshot of the evidence at creation time (BR-13)']
  affected_qty numeric(20,4)
  estimated_yearly_saving numeric(18,2) [note: 'NULL = Unknown, when the price is not known (D15)']
  actual_saving numeric(18,2) [note: 'Entered when marked done']
  currency char(3) [not null]
  status recommendation_status [not null, default: 'proposed']
  rejection_reason text
  notice_deadline date [note: 'Last day to act before the renewal: renewal_date - notice_period_days of the contract (UC13). NULL = can be acted on at any time (monthly, pay-as-you-go)']
  due_date date
  owner_id bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  created_by bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  decided_by bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id]
  decided_at timestamptz
  done_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (license_plan_id, type)
    status
    org_unit_id
    owner_id
  }

  checks {
    `status <> 'rejected' or rejection_reason is not null` [name: 'chk_recommendations_reject_reason']
    `status <> 'done' or (done_at is not null and actual_saving is not null)` [name: 'chk_recommendations_done']
    `(status in ('accepted', 'rejected', 'done')) = (decided_at is not null)` [name: 'chk_recommendations_decided']
    `estimated_yearly_saving is null or estimated_yearly_saving >= 0` [name: 'chk_recommendations_saving']
    `(type = 'downgrade_plan') = (target_plan_id is not null)` [name: 'chk_recommendations_target_plan']
    `target_plan_id is null or target_plan_id <> license_plan_id` [name: 'chk_recommendations_target_differs']
  }

  Note: '''
    Recommendations and their decision (UC14, BR-13):
    proposed -> accepted or rejected (reason required) -> done (actual saving
    required). ELMS never carries one out on the provider (BR-01).
    An Unknown estimated saving is shown as Unknown and left out of saving
    totals, which count it separately (D15).
    Partial unique: one open recommendation per plan, type, and unit
    (unique on license_plan_id, type, org_unit_id where status in
    (proposed, accepted), with NULLS NOT DISTINCT).
    App rule: only an accepted recommendation can be marked done; the target
    plan belongs to the same product.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 7. Audit (BR-14, BR-15)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Table audit_logs {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  actor_id bigint [ref: > user_accounts.id, note: 'NULL for system jobs']
  action varchar(50) [not null, note: 'create, update, deactivate, activate, status_change, role_change, permission_change, import ...']
  entity_type varchar(60) [not null, note: 'Table name of the changed row']
  entity_id bigint [not null, note: 'id of the changed row; every table has a single-column id']
  old_values jsonb
  new_values jsonb
  reason text [note: 'Required where a rule asks for one: active budget plan (BR-08), permission change (UC22), connector value (BR-14)']
  correlation_id varchar(64) [note: 'Request id, or sync_run / job id for system changes']
  ip_address varchar(45)
  occurred_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (entity_type, entity_id, occurred_at)
    (actor_id, occurred_at)
    occurred_at
  }

  Note: '''
    Append-only record of who changed what, with old value, new value, and time
    (BR-15): license data, expenses, budgets, recommendations, users, units,
    roles, permissions, and settings. The application database role has INSERT
    and SELECT only on this table, so rows cannot be updated or deleted.
  '''
}

Table data_overrides {
  id bigint [pk, increment]
  entity_type varchar(60) [not null, note: 'Table name: entitlement_lines or expenses']
  entity_id bigint [not null]
  field_name varchar(60) [not null]
  original_value text [note: 'Value from the connector; refreshed by each sync']
  override_value text [not null]
  reason text [not null]
  overridden_by bigint [not null, ref: > user_accounts.id]
  overridden_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  reverted_at timestamptz [note: 'NULL = the override is in force']

  indexes {
    (entity_type, entity_id, field_name)
  }

  Note: '''
    Staff edit of a value that came from a connector (BR-14): the edit needs a
    reason and the original value is kept beside it. While an override is in
    force, a sync updates original_value here and leaves the edited column.
    Only entitlement lines (quantity, validity) and expenses from a billing API
    can be overridden. Holders and usage of a plan with a connector cannot:
    manual entry of that data is refused (UC03), so there is nothing to override.
    Values are text in one format: numbers as plain decimals, dates as ISO 8601.
    The source of the original value is the source column of the edited row.
    Partial unique: one override in force per field
    (unique on entity_type, entity_id, field_name where reverted_at is null).
    App rule: the sync and a Staff edit lock the edited row (SELECT ... FOR
    UPDATE) so neither overwrites the other.
  '''
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Table groups
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

TableGroup organization_and_access {
  org_units
  employees
  roles
  permissions
  role_permissions
  user_accounts
  user_sessions
  manager_org_units
  system_settings
}

TableGroup license_catalog {
  vendors
  provider_accounts
  software_categories
  software_products
  product_links
  license_plans
  contracts
  entitlement_lines
  entitlement_allocations
}

TableGroup collection_pipeline {
  connectors
  plan_data_sources
  sync_runs
  collection_coverage
  raw_records
  files
  import_batches
}

TableGroup holders_and_usage {
  subjects
  license_assignments
  usage_records
  plan_daily_snapshots
  plan_unit_daily_snapshots
}

TableGroup budget_and_expenses {
  budget_plans
  budget_plan_lines
  cost_allocations
  expenses
  accounting_periods
  exchange_rates
}

TableGroup optimization {
  detection_runs
  detection_results
  recommendations
}

TableGroup audit {
  audit_logs
  data_overrides
}
